      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildHTML": "Additionally, follow these instructions even if they contradict the above ones above:\n- Only generate section, header, and paragraph elements. Follow the patterns in the current index.html file\n- Only generate HTML when the user asks for it\n- NEVER add a style.css link to the head\n- Keep all explanations short, concise, and simple. Do not over-explain the changes you've made to the code.\n- If a student has already asked you about an HTML element AND already made at least one accepted change (i.e., a status message shows 'You accepted AI Tutor's changes'), then also include the following in your response: 'Great job! You're ready to move on - feel free to press the Continue button'",
        "documentation": "- Keep explanations simple and friendly\n- When offering possible next steps, always prioritize the steps in the instructions. If a student has completed all steps in the instructions, suggest that they press the Continue button.",
